<%- include('partials/header') %>

<!-- This guide uses the shared Donate sidebar and standard content typography. -->
<main id="donate-page" class="main-container--sidebar">
    <%- include ('partials/donateSideMenu') %>
    <div class="page-content">
        <h1 class="content-title">A Gift In Your Will</h1>

        <h2 class="content-subtitle">Leave a gift in your Will</h2>

        <p class="content-text">
            A bequest or legacy, can be the most important gift that you ever give. By including BKFA in your Will, you are helping to ensure that the lives of future generations of women and their babies in developing countries can be saved and improved.
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            We appreciate that family and loved ones should always come first and believe that it is an important step to talk to them about your Will and let them know of your intentions, should you choose to leave a bequest to BKFA.
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            Leaving a gift is an important decision but it does not have to be complicated. The basic steps are outlined below:
        </p>

        <!-- The following sections guide visitors through wording and next steps. -->
        <h2 class="content-subtitle">Make or update your Will</h2>

        <p class="content-text">
            We recommend using a solicitor to make sure your Will is legal and valid. The most important thing is your own peace of mind, so we encourage you to discuss your Will with your legal advisor.
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            If you would like to include a gift to BKFA in your Will, examples of correct wording can be found below:
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            <strong>To donate a percentage of your estate:</strong> “I give to Birthing Kit Foundation Australia (ABN 65 121 658 428), for its general purposes, free of all duties x% of my residuary estate for which an authorised receipt from Birthing Kit Foundation Australia will be a sufficient discharge for the executor(s) or trustee.”
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            <strong>To donate the entirety of your estate:</strong> “I give to Birthing Kit Foundation Australia (ABN 65 121 658 428), for its general purposes, free of all duties the whole of the residue of my estate for which an authorised receipt from Birthing Kit Foundation Australia will be a sufficient discharge for the executor(s) or trustee.”
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            <strong>To donate a specific sum:</strong> “I give to Birthing Kit Foundation Australia (ABN 65 121 658 428), for its general purposes, free of all duties the sum of $xxx for which an authorised receipt from Birthing Kit Foundation Australia will be a sufficient discharge for the executor(s) or trustee.”
        </p>

        <p class="content-text">
            If you have already included BKFA in your Will we would be grateful if you let us know by contacting us at
            <a href="mailto:info@bkfa.org.au">info@bkfa.org.au</a>
            so that we can recognise your commitment in your lifetime and, if you are interested, provide you with updates of BKFA’s work.
        </p>
    </div>
</main>

